+# Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope; Cancelling It Is Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted. Amends [Deleting Records and Amending Booked Visits Are Deliberately Out of Scope](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) on NG-5 only.
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 declined every change to a visit once booked, and the 2026-08-08 ADR confirmed the row as a deliberate decision rather than a survey artifact. That ADR also set the terms for reopening it: a later request proceeds only on an explicit owner decision, and narrowing the row carries its own non-goal ADR.
+
+The owner has now made that decision (2026-09-09). Visits could be created and never corrected, so a mistyped date or description stayed wrong for good.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-5 whole.** Rejected: the owner decided otherwise, and a wrong record with no way back teaches nothing the sample needs to demonstrate.
+2. **Open the whole row.** Build correction and cancellation together. Rejected: cancellation is the part that adds lifecycle state, which is what the original rationale objected to.
+3. **Narrow the row to cancellation** (chosen). Correcting a booked visit's date and description is in scope; cancelling one is not.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-5 covers cancelling a booked visit. Correcting a booked visit's date and description is in scope as REQ-VIS-003.
+
+The owner's decision, quoted from the intake record:
+
+> Non-goal NG-5 is narrowed: cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope, but correcting its date and description is now in. Record the narrowing the way the project records non-goal changes.
+
+The rationale the narrowing keeps is the lifecycle one. A correction overwrites what a visit says; a cancellation would give a visit a state it can be in, which the sample models nowhere.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The sample no longer corrects records forward only for owners and pets. A booked visit is mutable in its date and its description.
+- NG-4 is untouched. Deleting a visit stays out of scope, and cancellation has no home in either row's exception.
+- Widening NG-5 further — cancellation, or a visit's lifecycle state — is a fresh owner decision with its own ADR.
+- The correction has no link into it from the owner's record. The owner named a visible entry point as a possible follow-up, recorded as an open question in the PRD.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [REQ-VIS-003](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the capability the narrowing admits.
